{"title":"2021 GCIME Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693237ed05c75d0b63b81fdb9afda7555cb15bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> denote the number of primes less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c544b03d97acd864d1fe1d84d1180f05eb53cc23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi(a)^{\\pi(b)}=\\pi(b)^{\\pi(a)}=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"20\" />. For some fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> what is the maximum possible number of solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80414f2f94f70731e91b6e12c4e6934c8fa65de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> but not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> denote the number of solutions to the given equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/7/b375254d0509a5faf27792d31df212877b13f541.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor\\sqrt{n}\\rfloor+\\lfloor\\sqrt[3]{n}\\rfloor+\\lfloor\\sqrt[4]{n}\\lfloor+\\lfloor\\sqrt[5]{n}\\rfloor=100\\]\" width=\"277\" height=\"20\" /> What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a cyclic kite. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb0f1923c633ea756a97320cd000c57e0f82bab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\in\\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> be the inradius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/04805d6e3b4443f1475007a2a1d52695a0acab9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\cdot BC\\cdot r$\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> is a perfect square. What is the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/04805d6e3b4443f1475007a2a1d52695a0acab9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\cdot BC\\cdot r$\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/9129cc5dc095eb711e728c4241a0fc5104c3cec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> as the harmonic mean of all the divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. Find the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252c40a396f23708ea7b91e2623cc53722be09a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d20796143abf0ee50c2108cb351f9430408363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{H(n)}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"38\" /> is the minimum amongst all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252bb71621f0c276648f222830977f52ea3fcc6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;n\\leq 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be a real number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/dda5fdb63c044fe31a5027b6a71f1c2938524f4e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin^{4}x}{20}+\\frac{\\cos^{4}x}{21}=\\frac{1}{41}\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"41\" /> If the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d35a761fff5e6b43c81a99fe98c5fa74fd567d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin^{6}x}{20^{3}}+\\frac{\\cos^{6}x}{21^{3}}\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"41\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c80f7cbc6e8017ab735d473c6f3eb2e66a40511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, then what is the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two scales used to measure temperature are degrees Fahrenheit (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) and degrees Celsius (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) and the two are related by the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7daaea88f6235de4577b216292b38c6daee7766b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F=\\tfrac{9}{5}C+32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"103\" height=\"21\" />. When a two-digit integer degree temperature <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> in Celcius is converted to Fahrenheit and rounded to the nearest integer degree, it turns out the ones and tens digits of the original Celsius temperature\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sometimes switch places to give the rounded Fahrenheit equivalent. Find the sum of all two-digit integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which this happens.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd28b278a07bda0ea4d08737743613980c6aa6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> denote the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/6/006eb96d9bd52ddc8839d0e664845d452c435cdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${{(4n)^{(3n)}}^{(2n)}}^{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"26\" />. Then find the sum of all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252c40a396f23708ea7b91e2623cc53722be09a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/67417575fe5b6494bbcc1c6833664e36cdf08a98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_{i}&lt;4n.\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A basketball club decided to label every basketball in the club. After labeling all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> of the balls, the labeler noticed that exactly half of the balls had the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Find the sum of all possible three-digit integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12e13563a6df1a207dad9672dd7b73df2a96faa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/2782ccf4ca9cf31227fb7efa5433ce62f2739f36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, AC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. If the circumcircles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55b55a6a8b5c540e2175e9b9f8576112f45be3d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFE, \\triangle BFD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/d/18d6098ce09f6f2b36bb447d30083315c8c0ca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CED$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> all pass through the orthocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/8/a783f6df112953438e7fb2b04d6821873c44ea76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> then the maximum possible area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/cccc0e0c9eede590ec438e70a40ae20ec0a3f057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\sqrt{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> for squarefree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b56d32444d8efd65eb0cb6c01f8ac72c32587e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be randomly chosen real numbers from the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/6064c48dbe7569d0efa8663bd6c9eb7d6fc62846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-10, 10]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. Let the probability that these randomly chosen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b56d32444d8efd65eb0cb6c01f8ac72c32587e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> satisfy the following inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e66314caedb71759fb8c639f3d3648dba257f9a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10(|x|+|y|+|z|)\\geq 100\\geq x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2}\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"19\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac0fbf2167982a1c6fa927f89ef11051979a372.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m\\pi-n}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f4bf5eb49eb976370c998db03e26d528d21dd3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a61870035304b46bdbcafc39d04bea20e3899c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_GCIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 GCIME Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018063715\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 339/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\